  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Line-dance music of Lebanon, Syria, Palestine and Jordan, played at village weddings for centuries and turned into an amplified cassette genre from the 1980s by Syrian and Palestinian wedding singers such as Omar Souleyman, Ali El Deek and Samir Shukri — mijwiz or arghul double-clarinet riffs, later Korg keyboards imitating them, over tabl and derbouka driving a stamping 4/4 or 6/8 at 100-160 BPM, with maqam-based sung couplets and shouted ataba and mijana vocal preludes.",
